times: Among members of a congregation only (group: congregation; the rate is the yearly rate among members): public vows, to give up drink, to serve or to give, are an old rite in many faiths, often made after a hard year (estimate); a vow tested in the keeping comes to about 1 in 4 members, set at 8 in 1,000 a year for young adults and less after
likelier: a hard year behind them, a drinking habit that worried the family, an elder who has taken them under their wing
rarer: a member in name only, a person who makes no promises they might not keep
