horizon: years
roles: friend, elder, grandparent
who: elder
earth: in front of the whole congregation you vowed a year without drink, it is month four, and your oldest friend's birthday is on Saturday
scene: After last winter's trouble, {N} stood up at the gathering and vowed before everyone: a year without a drop of drink. It is month four, {friend}'s birthday is on Saturday, and the whole congregation knows the vow.
scene W: A vow said before the gathering binds, and {N} has never yet broken one.
scene U: {N} keeps asking whether a vow made in a bad week still binds the person {N} is now.
scene B: Keeping it would make {N} someone the elders trust with real responsibility. Breaking it would be remembered.
scene R: The birthday is going to be wild, and {N} can already taste the first glass.
scene G: {grandparent} made the same vow at {Ns} age, and kept it for forty years.
